WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.400
Take a move we could never pull off handheld:
flying right through one of the holes in this board.

00:04.400 --> 00:09.000
We drop keyframe A, set up a dolly zoom into B,
place C right before the hole,

00:09.000 --> 00:13.400
and push D straight through the opening.

00:13.400 --> 00:17.000
Stepping back, we can see the whole move:
the app connects all our preset stretches—

00:17.000 --> 00:20.000
from dollies to pushes—into one continuous camera path.

00:20.000 --> 00:24.000
We can also plan the timing and speed of the camera.
Let's speed up that dolly zoom movement.

00:24.000 --> 00:28.000
We can adjust the total duration,
tweak the easing across each segment,

00:28.000 --> 00:32.500
and fine-tune the speed curves
so the camera slows down and speeds up.

00:37.000 --> 00:43.000
Next is capture. Since the phone can't fit through the plastic,
we take an offset pass right over the top.

00:43.000 --> 00:47.000
We just follow the AR guidance casually,
and if we deviate too much,

00:47.000 --> 00:51.000
on-screen prompts steer us right back on track.

00:51.000 --> 00:55.000
In review, we scrub between what we captured and our target path.

00:55.000 --> 00:59.000
As we pull the slider all the way to target,
we can see some missing coverage in red.

00:59.000 --> 01:03.800
Tapping that area launches AR guidance for a pickup,
showing us exactly where to aim the camera
to grab the missing evidence.
